                [ 'p', 'xTool frames and screens come in two sizes: 228 × 304 mm for cards and small canvases, and 292 × 406 mm for T-shirts, bags and canvases up to 279 × 356 mm. Mugs, bottles and strongly curved surfaces are out of reach for this kit – UV printing or engraving with a rotary attachment suits them better.' ],
                [ 'p', 'Screens come in 100 or 200 mesh. The denser 200 mesh holds fine text and thin lines better, while 100 mesh has larger openings that are harder to clog – that is the mesh xTool specifies for its photochromic and thermochromic inks.' ],
